      "final_text": "Done \u2014 `check_candidate` returns `VERIFIED` on all 8 requirements, and `verify_passport` reproduces it.\n\n**Fix:** the candidate ran 6 Newton steps instead of the deployed 7, which understated the root on large inputs (e.g. `2^256 - 1`). [Solution.lean](candidate/Solution.lean) now runs the full 7-step OpenZeppelin `Math.sqrt` loop (`1 << (log2(a) >> 1)`, 7 Newton lines, `min(result, a / result)`).\n\n**Proof outline:**\n- `req_newton_budget`: the 7-let body is `newtonSqrt 7` after unfolding (`simp only [sqrt, newtonSqrt, iterate, newtonStep]`).\n- Core lemma `sqrt_toNat`: `(sqrt a).toNat = Nat.sqrt a.toNat`. The initial estimate is `2^(log2/2)`, within a factor of 2 of the root; each BitVec Newton step is overflow-free (sums stay below `2^256`, iterates below `2^129`) so it matches Nat `newton`; 7 steps reach the root or root-plus-one (`newtonIter_eq_or_succ_of_lt_two_mul` with `b=128, k=5`), and `min(result, a/result)` selects the root (`min_div_eq_sqrt`).\n- The other 7 requirements follow: floor bounds from `Nat.sqrt_le`/`Nat.lt_succ_sqrt`, `sqrtUp` facts from the rounded-up root lemmas, and the three mint requirements from `firstMint_eq_some`/`firstMint_isSome` plus the floor.\n\nPassport: `.proofforge/passport-001.json`, sha256 `edfffcaa5bcfd55339246c17152687444aa68d615ecd8ebb1b715d816df8ef6a`. Only `candidate/Solution.lean` was changed.",
